 ## Configuration

+### Exit policy and baselines
+
+`run` and two-tier evaluation return `0` for passing checks, `12` for failed
+assertions, and `13` for runner or scorer errors. Explicit `EVAL_WARN_ONLY=1`
+changes only assertion failures to exit `0`. It never suppresses errors.
+`EVAL_BYPASS=1` explicitly skips evaluation and logs a bypass event.
+
+`baseline` and `accept` can record failed assertions when explicitly requested.
+This does not exempt those assertions from future failures. Neither command
+accepts runner or scorer errors, including errors in stability samples or
+repetitions when the primary attempt passed. Baseline creation requires results
+from the run it just executed; a skipped run cannot reuse an older result.
+
+`promote` is no longer required and does not change saved state. To stop using
+explicit warning mode, unset `EVAL_WARN_ONLY`.
+
